WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.431 --> 00:00:03.541
- I can see someone I knew as a child

00:00:03.541 --> 00:00:06.901
and immediately recognize
them as an adult,

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.432
or I can see someone who worked at a store

00:00:09.432 --> 00:00:11.575
that I used to go to 10 years ago,

00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:15.742
and see them on the street and
recognize them as that clerk.

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:20.281
My name is Jennifer Jarrett,
and I'm a super recognizer.

00:00:20.281 --> 00:00:21.879
I remember just about every face I see.

00:00:21.879 --> 00:00:24.134
I don't have to have
an emotional attachment

00:00:24.134 --> 00:00:26.247
to people to remember them.

00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:28.977
I really started to recognize
it when I went to college.

00:00:28.977 --> 00:00:31.332
I would meet people, I
would always remember them,

00:00:31.332 --> 00:00:32.978
and then a couple of months later,

00:00:32.978 --> 00:00:34.550
I'd be at a party and people would say,

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:35.726
"Oh, do you two know each other?"

00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:38.358
and I'd say yes, and the
other person would say no.

00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:39.380
So, then, I sort of started

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.529
to learn what was a memorable
encounter and what wasn't.

00:00:42.529 --> 00:00:44.481
In terms of being a super recognizer,

00:00:44.481 --> 00:00:47.841
so far I haven't really
found any way to utilize it.

00:00:47.841 --> 00:00:51.408
At my last college reunion,
my friends were so excited

00:00:51.408 --> 00:00:52.963
because, you know, everybody worries

00:00:52.963 --> 00:00:54.322
that they're gonna go to a reunion

00:00:54.322 --> 00:00:56.043
and not remember who people are,

00:00:56.043 --> 00:00:58.940
so people were sticking to me like glue

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.896
so I could tell everyone
who was in the room.

00:01:01.896 --> 00:01:05.646
(gentle instrumental music)

